  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD &amp; EC Funded Unlocking the Potential of the Moringa Cake project - CAFOD Held Grant</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This proposal is aimed at directly addressing both short and long term income and food insecurity of vulnerable Sierra Leoneans in Kenema and Bombali Districts. This will be done through the sustainable development of small scale poultry and inland fisheries production schemes. The project intends to use innovative and locally appropriate approaches and technologies to improve production in both poultry and fish farming as a way of enhancing communities livelihoods options. It will benefit vulnerable populations, especially women and youth affected by years of conflict in Sierra Leone thereby contributing to the realisation of MDG 1 (i.e. Eradicate Extreme Poverty and Hunger) and support youth employment initiatives in the Country. 
Capacities of local partners and selected communities in Bombali and Kenema districts will be enhanced to enable them pilot innovative, cost effective and locally appropriate initiatives aimed at increasing production, value addition, consumption and marketing of fresh water fish and poultry.</narrative>
  </description>
